  "details": "- CVE-2026-14257: bound the total number of characters brace expansion may\n  accumulate in the bundled npm brace-expansion copies, so chained brace\n  groups can no longer grow every result until the process dies with an\n  uncatchable out-of-memory error\n- CVE-2026-59874: refuse a negative entry size in the bundled npm node-tar\n  copy, both when decoding a base-256 header field and when parsing a pax\n  size record, so a crafted archive can no longer stall tar.replace on a\n  scan that never advances past the same header\n- CVE-2026-69152: charge the intermediate arrays built for comma\n  alternatives and padded sequences against that same length budget,\n  closing a bypass that exhausted memory before the CVE-2026-14257 bound\n  could take effect",
